\newlabel{tab:six-rooms}{{4}{13}{Targets under 50\,cm in six held-out rooms (543 in total). Box overlap: correctly placed when $\operatorname {IoU}_{3\mathrm {D}}\ge 0.25$ replaces Eq.~\ref {eq:center-size}; the next two columns use Eq.~\ref {eq:center-size}. Instances: reconstructed objects of any size, excluding structure. Matching: share of them that match an annotated target. Time and estimated driving-agent cost are per room. The last two rows score an inventory's boxes directly, with no agent}{table.4}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Per-room difference in targets under 50\,cm correctly placed. Rooms are numbered in evaluation order, with their target counts. $p$: exact two-sided sign-flip test over rooms; with six rooms it cannot fall below 0.031.}}{14}{table.5}\protected@file@percent }
